{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "overview",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# SignSage: dual-model ISL training\n",
    "\n",
    "Train isolated-sign recognition and continuous pose-to-English translation as separate experiments. This notebook is self-contained, uses PyTorch, and exports backend-shaped research bundles. No real training or downloads start unless an enable flag is changed.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run cells top to bottom. First code cell is configuration only. Attach datasets through Kaggle **Add data** or set local paths; do not attach raw data to output bundles. Models trained here are experimental and are not promoted or avatar-signing systems.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Pipelines\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Isolated signs: video or prepared `(T, 543, 3)` pose sequence → one dataset-specific word label.\n",
    "2. Continuous translation: aligned `.pose`/pose sequence → English target sentence.\n",
    "\n",
    "Never combine vocabularies across datasets. iSign text is sentence translation data, not an isolated-sign class map."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dataset-evidence",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Dataset evidence and attachment policy\n",
    "\n",
    "Metadata verified from official dataset cards, Hugging Face repositories, and Mendeley/DataCite DOI records. Datasets must be attached manually via Kaggle **Add data** or mapped to local paths; this notebook never performs automated multi-gigabyte downloads.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Dataset | Verified Metadata & License | Role in Dual Pipeline | 543-Landmark Preprocessing & Conversion Requirement |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| [GloSL-ISL](https://huggingface.co/datasets/pedroodb/glosl-isl) | Public HF repository; 126,846 rows; `annotations.csv` (`id, split, text, signer, video_ref, pose_file`); CC BY-NC 4.0; null signer metadata. | Primary Model B (Translation) reader. Research-only opt-in. | Native 543-point MediaPipe Holistic `.pose` files. Attach uncompressed folder containing `annotations.csv` and `poses/`. |\n",
    "| [iSign](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Exploration-Lab/iSign) | Gated HF repository; CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; `uid,text` annotations with large multipart pose archives. | Optional Model B (Translation) reader. Requires HF approval. | Native MediaPipe `.pose` files named `<uid>.pose`. Attach extracted pose directory and CSV. UIDs are sample IDs; video grouping is sample-independent unless explicit `video_id` metadata is supplied. |\n",
    "| [ISL-CSLTR](https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/kcmpdxky7p/1) | Mendeley Data (DOI 10.17632/kcmpdxky7p.1); CC BY 4.0; 700 continuous videos, 100 sentences, 7 signers. | Candidate Model B (Translation) dataset. | Raw video files (.mp4). Requires MediaPipe Holistic extraction to generate (T, 543, 3) landmarks. Supported via built-in `convert_isl_csltr_to_canonical_manifest()`. |\n",
    "| [CISLR](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Exploration-Lab/CISLR) | Gated HF repository (AFL-3.0); word-level recognition; raw video archives + 1024-D I3D features. | Candidate Model A (Recognition) dataset. | **Important**: Pre-extracted I3D features from CISLR are 1024-D visual features, NOT 543-point skeletal landmarks. To use SignSage's skeletal pipeline, raw videos must be processed via MediaPipe Holistic into (T, 543, 3) format. |\n",
    "| [Amrita SLR](https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/dtg9s785v8/1) | Mendeley Data (DOI 10.17632/dtg9s785v8/1); CC BY 4.0 (embargoed access); 50 signs, ~16 clips/class, 7 signers. | Candidate Model A (Recognition) dataset. | 1080p 28 FPS raw video files. Requires MediaPipe Holistic landmark extraction to produce 543-point arrays before isolated-word training. |\n",
    "| [INCLUDE](https://huggingface.co/datasets/manojkumarcs/INCLUDE_Dataset) | Ungated HF repository (~56 GB); 4,292 videos / 263 signs; **no license declaration** found. | **Disabled by policy** until licensing terms are verified. | Do not download or train until copyright terms are officially declared. |\n",
    "\n",
    "### 543-Landmark Preprocessing Contract\n",
    "\n",
    "SignSage enforces a unified skeletal representation across all pipelines:\n",
    "- **Total Landmarks**: 543 3D coordinates `(x, y, z)` ordered strictly as:\n",
    "  - `POSE_LANDMARKS` [0:33] (33 points)\n",
    "  - `FACE_LANDMARKS` [33:501] (468 points)\n",
    "  - `LEFT_HAND_LANDMARKS` [501:522] (21 points)\n",
    "  - `RIGHT_HAND_LANDMARKS` [522:543] (21 points)\n",
    "- **Model A (Recognition)**: Slices body pose [0:33] and both hands [501:543] (75 points = 225 features), normalizes by centering on hip midpoint and scaling by shoulder width, resamples to 64 frames.\n",
    "- **Model B (Translation)**: Normalizes all 543 landmarks (1629 features), resizes to `MAX_FRAMES` (160), and concatenates frame-to-frame velocity deltas in `FrameProjection` (3258 input dim).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Pilot vs. Full Training Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "- `TRAINING_MODE = \"pilot\"`: Restricts training and evaluation to a deterministic subset (`MAX_SAMPLES_PER_SPLIT = 256`) for rapid verification in Kaggle sessions. Exported artifacts are explicitly tagged `scope: \"pilot_subset\"`.\n",
    "- `TRAINING_MODE = \"full\"`: Sets `MAX_SAMPLES_PER_SPLIT = 0` to train on the entire attached dataset. Exported artifacts are tagged `scope: \"full_dataset\"`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "configuration",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import csv\n",
    "import hashlib\n",
    "import itertools\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import math\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import random\n",
    "import tempfile\n",
    "from collections import Counter, defaultdict\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "from torch import nn\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, Dataset, TensorDataset\n",
    "\n",
    "SEED = 42\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE = 8\n",
    "EPOCHS = 3\n",
    "LEARNING_RATE = 3e-4\n",
    "\n",
    "# TRAINING MODE CONFIGURATION\n",
    "# Set TRAINING_MODE = \"pilot\" for fast smoke checks (bounded by MAX_SAMPLES_PER_SPLIT).\n",
    "# Set TRAINING_MODE = \"full\" for complete dataset training across all available rows.\n",
    "TRAINING_MODE = \"pilot\"  # \"pilot\" | \"full\"\n",
    "MAX_SAMPLES_PER_SPLIT = 256 if TRAINING_MODE == \"pilot\" else 0\n",
    "TRAINING_SCOPE = \"pilot_subset\" if (TRAINING_MODE == \"pilot\" and MAX_SAMPLES_PER_SPLIT > 0) else \"full_dataset\"\n",
    "\n",
    "MAX_FRAMES = 160\n",
    "MAX_TOKENS = 96\n",
    "SP_VOCAB_SIZE = 4000\n",
    "MODEL_DIM = 128\n",
    "ATTENTION_HEADS = 4\n",
    "TRANSFORMER_LAYERS = 2\n",
    "FEED_FORWARD_DIM = 512\n",
    "\n",
    "TRAIN_RECOGNITION = False\n",
    "TRAIN_TRANSLATION = False\n",
    "RESUME_RECOGNITION = False\n",
    "RESUME_TRANSLATION = False\n",
    "RUN_SYNTHETIC_SMOKE = True\n",
    "CONFIRM_DATASET_RIGHTS = False\n",
    "ALLOW_RESEARCH_ONLY_DATASETS = False\n",
    "\n",
    "ISOLATED_MANIFEST = None  # e.g. Path(\"/kaggle/input/my-signs/manifest.csv\")\n",
    "ISOLATED_DATA_ROOT = Path(\"/kaggle/input\")\n",
    "ISOLATED_PATH_COLUMN = \"path\"\n",
    "ISOLATED_LABEL_COLUMN = \"label\"\n",
    "ISOLATED_VIDEO_COLUMN = \"video_id\"\n",
    "ISOLATED_SIGNER_COLUMN = \"signer\"  # set \"\" when absent\n",
    "ISOLATED_DATASET_NAME = \"local isolated-sign dataset\"\n",
    "ISOLATED_LICENSE = \"unverified\"\n",
    "\n",
    "TRANSLATION_MANIFEST = None  # GloSL annotations.csv, iSign uid/text CSV, or canonical CSV.\n",
    "TRANSLATION_POSE_ROOT = Path(\"/kaggle/input\")\n",
    "TRANSLATION_FORMAT = \"auto\"  # auto | glosl | isign | canonical\n",
    "TRANSLATION_DATASET_NAME = \"GloSL-ISL\"\n",
    "TRANSLATION_LICENSE = \"CC BY-NC 4.0\"\n",
    "\n",
    "OUTPUT_ROOT = Path(\"/kaggle/working/outputs\") if Path(\"/kaggle/working\").exists() else Path(\"outputs\")\n",
    "DEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
    "\n",
    "random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "np.random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n",
    "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(SEED)\n",
    "torch.backends.cudnn.benchmark = False\n",
    "torch.backends.cudnn.deterministic = True\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"device={DEVICE}; seed={SEED}; outputs={OUTPUT_ROOT.resolve()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"training_mode={TRAINING_MODE}; scope={TRAINING_SCOPE}; max_samples_per_split={MAX_SAMPLES_PER_SPLIT}\")\n",
    "print(f\"train_recognition={TRAIN_RECOGNITION}; train_translation={TRAIN_TRANSLATION}\")\n",
    "if (BATCH_SIZE < 1 or EPOCHS < 1 or MAX_SAMPLES_PER_SPLIT < 0\n",
    "        or MAX_FRAMES < 2 or MAX_TOKENS < 3 or MODEL_DIM % ATTENTION_HEADS):\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\"Invalid training config: check batch/epoch counts, sample cap, sequence lengths, and attention dimensions.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "data-loading",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2–3. Dataset loading, validation, and splits\n",
    "\n",
    "Readers accept explicit local paths only. Translation `.pose` layout is checked before positional landmark slicing. Video extraction preserves frame order and uses the SignSage order: pose, face, left hand, right hand."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "data-functions",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "TOTAL_LANDMARKS = 543\n",
    "RAW_FEATURE_DIM = 1629\n",
    "COMPONENT_ORDER = [\"POSE_LANDMARKS\", \"FACE_LANDMARKS\", \"LEFT_HAND_LANDMARKS\", \"RIGHT_HAND_LANDMARKS\"]\n",
    "COMPONENT_RANGES = {\n",
    "    \"POSE_LANDMARKS\": [0, 33], \"FACE_LANDMARKS\": [33, 501],\n",
    "    \"LEFT_HAND_LANDMARKS\": [501, 522], \"RIGHT_HAND_LANDMARKS\": [522, 543],\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def read_csv_rows(path):\n",
    "    path = Path(path)\n",
    "    if not path.is_file():\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Dataset CSV not found: {path}\")\n",
    "    with path.open(newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8-sig\") as stream:\n",
    "        reader = csv.DictReader(stream)\n",
    "        rows = list(reader)\n",
    "        fields = reader.fieldnames or []\n",
    "    if not rows:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"No data rows in {path}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"{path}: {len(rows):,} rows; fields={fields}\")\n",
    "    return rows, fields\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def show_input_tree(root, limit=20):\n",
    "    root = Path(root)\n",
    "    if not root.exists():\n",
    "        print(f\"Input root unavailable: {root}\")\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    sample = [p.relative_to(root).as_posix() for p in itertools.islice(\n",
    "        (p for p in root.rglob(\"*\") if p.is_file()), limit\n",
    "    )]\n",
    "    print(f\"{root}: sample files={sample}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def validate_landmarks(sequence, source):\n",
    "    arr = np.asarray(sequence)\n",
    "    if arr.ndim != 3 or arr.shape[1:] != (TOTAL_LANDMARKS, 3):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"{source}: expected (T,543,3), received {arr.shape}\")\n",
    "    if len(arr) < 2:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"{source}: need at least two frames\")\n",
    "    if arr.dtype.kind not in \"iuf\" or not np.isfinite(arr).all():\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"{source}: landmarks must be numeric and finite\")\n",
    "    return arr.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _read_pose_format(path):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        from pose_format import Pose\n",
    "    except ImportError as exc:\n",
    "        raise ImportError(\"Reading .pose requires `pip install pose-format`.\") from exc\n",
    "    pose = Pose.read(Path(path).read_bytes())\n",
    "    names = [component.name for component in pose.header.components]\n",
    "    points = sum(len(component.points) for component in pose.header.components)\n",
    "    if names[:len(COMPONENT_ORDER)] != COMPONENT_ORDER or points < TOTAL_LANDMARKS:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"{path}: incompatible pose header; components={names}, points={points}\")\n",
    "    data = np.asarray(np.ma.filled(pose.body.data, 0.0), dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "    if data.ndim != 4 or data.shape[1] < 1 or data.shape[2] < TOTAL_LANDMARKS or data.shape[3] < 3:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"{path}: unexpected pose tensor shape {data.shape}\")\n",
    "    return validate_landmarks(data[:, 0, :TOTAL_LANDMARKS, :3], path)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _video_landmarks(path):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import cv2\n",
    "        import mediapipe as mp\n",
    "    except ImportError as exc:\n",
    "        raise ImportError(\"Video extraction requires `pip install mediapipe opencv-python-headless`.\") from exc\n",
    "    cap = cv2.VideoCapture(str(path))\n",
    "    if not cap.isOpened():\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"Cannot open video: {path}\")\n",
    "    sequences = []\n",
    "    def points_or_zeros(component, count):\n",
    "        if component is None:\n",
    "            return np.zeros((count, 3), dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "        points = np.asarray([[p.x, p.y, p.z] for p in component.landmark], dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "        if points.shape != (count, 3):\n",
    "            raise ValueError(f\"Unexpected MediaPipe component shape {points.shape}; expected {(count, 3)}\")\n",
    "        return points\n",
    "    with mp.solutions.holistic.Holistic(\n",
    "        static_image_mode=False, model_complexity=1,\n",
    "        enable_segmentation=False, refine_face_landmarks=False,\n",
    "    ) as holistic:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            while True:\n",
    "                ok, frame = cap.read()\n",
    "                if not ok:\n",
    "                    break\n",
    "                result = holistic.process(cv2.cvtColor(frame, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\n",
    "                sequences.append(np.concatenate([\n",
    "                    points_or_zeros(result.pose_landmarks, 33),\n",
    "                    points_or_zeros(result.face_landmarks, 468),\n",
    "                    points_or_zeros(result.left_hand_landmarks, 21),\n",
    "                    points_or_zeros(result.right_hand_landmarks, 21),\n",
    "                ], axis=0))\n",
    "        finally:\n",
    "            cap.release()\n",
    "    return validate_landmarks(np.asarray(sequences), path)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_landmarks(path, cache_dir=None):\n",
    "    path = Path(path)\n",
    "    if not path.is_file():\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Sample file not found: {path}\")\n",
    "    suffix = path.suffix.lower()\n",
    "    if suffix == \".pose\":\n",
    "        return _read_pose_format(path)\n",
    "    if suffix in (\".mp4\", \".mov\", \".avi\", \".mkv\"):\n",
    "        if cache_dir is None:\n",
    "            return _video_landmarks(path)\n",
    "        cache_dir = Path(cache_dir)\n",
    "        cache_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "        stat = path.stat()\n",
    "        key = hashlib.sha256(f\"{path.resolve()}:{stat.st_size}:{stat.st_mtime_ns}\".encode()).hexdigest()\n",
    "        cached = cache_dir / f\"{key}.npy\"\n",
    "        if not cached.exists():\n",
    "            np.save(cached, _video_landmarks(path))\n",
    "        return validate_landmarks(np.load(cached, allow_pickle=False), path)\n",
    "    if suffix == \".npy\":\n",
    "        return validate_landmarks(np.load(path, allow_pickle=False), path)\n",
    "    if suffix == \".npz\":\n",
    "        with np.load(path, allow_pickle=False) as archive:\n",
    "            candidates = [k for k in (\"landmarks\", \"pose\", \"poses\") if k in archive]\n",
    "            if not candidates:\n",
    "                raise ValueError(f\"{path}: .npz must contain landmarks, pose, or poses\")\n",
    "            return validate_landmarks(archive[candidates[0]], path)\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported sample format {suffix!r}: {path}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def normalize_pose_sequence(flat):\n",
    "    arr = np.asarray(flat)\n",
    "    if arr.ndim != 2 or arr.shape[1] != RAW_FEATURE_DIM or arr.dtype.kind not in \"iuf\":\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"Expected numeric (T,1629) input, received {arr.shape}/{arr.dtype}\")\n",
    "    x = arr.reshape(len(arr), TOTAL_LANDMARKS, 3).astype(np.float32)\n",
    "    with np.errstate(invalid=\"ignore\"):\n",
    "        center = np.nanmean(x[:, [23, 24], :], axis=1, keepdims=True)\n",
    "    bad = ~np.isfinite(center).all(axis=(1, 2))\n",
    "    if bad.any():\n",
    "        with np.errstate(invalid=\"ignore\"):\n",
    "            center[bad] = np.nanmean(x[bad, :33, :], axis=1, keepdims=True)\n",
    "    x -= center\n",
    "    with np.errstate(invalid=\"ignore\"):\n",
    "        scales = np.nanstd(x[:, :33, :].reshape(len(x), -1), axis=1)\n",
    "    valid = scales[np.isfinite(scales) & (scales > 1e-6)]\n",
    "    scale = float(np.nanmedian(valid)) if len(valid) else 1.0\n",
    "    if not math.isfinite(scale) or scale <= 1e-6:\n",
    "        scale = 1.0\n",
    "    return np.nan_to_num(x / scale, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0).reshape(len(x), -1).astype(np.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def resize_sequence(sequence, target_len):\n",
    "    seq = np.asarray(sequence)\n",
    "    if seq.ndim != 2 or not len(seq):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"Expected non-empty (T,D) sequence, got {seq.shape}\")\n",
    "    if len(seq) > target_len:\n",
    "        idx = np.linspace(0, len(seq) - 1, target_len).round().astype(np.int64)\n",
    "        return seq[idx].astype(np.float32), target_len\n",
    "    out = np.zeros((target_len, seq.shape[1]), dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "    out[:len(seq)] = seq\n",
    "    return out, len(seq)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def resolve_input_path(value, root):\n",
    "    candidate = Path(str(value))\n",
    "    return candidate if candidate.is_absolute() else Path(root) / candidate\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def split_grouped(records, group_key, seed=SEED):\n",
    "    groups = defaultdict(list)\n",
    "    for row in records:\n",
    "        group = str(row.get(group_key, \"\")).strip()\n",
    "        if not group:\n",
    "            raise ValueError(f\"Missing group value for {group_key}; refusing leaky split.\")\n",
    "        groups[group].append(row)\n",
    "    if len(groups) < 3:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"Need at least three independent {group_key} groups; found {len(groups)}\")\n",
    "    keys = list(groups)\n",
    "    random.Random(seed).shuffle(keys)\n",
    "    targets = {\"train\": 0.8, \"validation\": 0.1, \"test\": 0.1}\n",
    "    result = {name: [] for name in targets}\n",
    "    total = sum(len(rows) for rows in groups.values())\n",
    "    for group in keys:\n",
    "        name = min(targets, key=lambda key: len(result[key]) / max(targets[key] * total, 1))\n",
    "        result[name].extend(groups[group])\n",
    "    all_groups = {name: {r[group_key] for r in rows} for name, rows in result.items()}\n",
    "    if (all_groups[\"train\"] & all_groups[\"validation\"] or\n",
    "        all_groups[\"train\"] & all_groups[\"test\"] or\n",
    "        all_groups[\"validation\"] & all_groups[\"test\"]):\n",
    "        raise AssertionError(f\"Group leakage in {group_key} split\")\n",
    "    return result\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def limit_split(rows, limit, seed):\n",
    "    if not limit or len(rows) <= limit:\n",
    "        return rows\n",
    "    return random.Random(seed).sample(rows, limit)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def fingerprint_rows(rows, fields):\n",
    "    payload = [[str(row.get(field, \"\")) for field in fields] for row in rows]\n",
    "    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(\",\", \":\")).encode()).hexdigest()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def prepare_isolated_features(landmarks):\n",
    "    arr = validate_landmarks(landmarks, \"recognition sample\")\n",
    "    selected = arr[:, list(range(33)) + list(range(501, 543)), :]\n",
    "    hips = (selected[:, 23] + selected[:, 24]) * 0.5\n",
    "    shoulder = np.linalg.norm(selected[:, 11, :2] - selected[:, 12, :2], axis=1)\n",
    "    valid = shoulder[shoulder > 1e-5]\n",
    "    scale = float(np.median(valid)) if len(valid) else 1.0\n",
    "    selected = (selected - hips[:, None, :]) / scale\n",
    "    indices = np.linspace(0, len(selected) - 1, 64).round().astype(int)\n",
    "    features = selected[indices].reshape(64, 225).astype(np.float32)\n",
    "    if not np.isfinite(features).all():\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"Non-finite recognition features\")\n",
    "    return features\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_isolated_records():\n",
    "    if ISOLATED_MANIFEST is None:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"Set ISOLATED_MANIFEST to an attached CSV before enabling recognition.\")\n",
    "    rows, fields = read_csv_rows(ISOLATED_MANIFEST)\n",
    "    required = {ISOLATED_PATH_COLUMN, ISOLATED_LABEL_COLUMN}\n",
    "    if not required.issubset(fields):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"Recognition manifest missing columns {sorted(required - set(fields))}; found {fields}\")\n",
    "    show_input_tree(ISOLATED_DATA_ROOT)\n",
    "    records, errors = [], []\n",
    "    for index, row in enumerate(rows):\n",
    "        label = str(row.get(ISOLATED_LABEL_COLUMN, \"\")).strip()\n",
    "        path = resolve_input_path(row.get(ISOLATED_PATH_COLUMN, \"\"), ISOLATED_DATA_ROOT)\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            if not label:\n",
    "                raise ValueError(\"empty sign label\")\n",
    "            features = prepare_isolated_features(load_landmarks(path, OUTPUT_ROOT / \"cache\" / \"video_poses\"))\n",
    "            video = str(row.get(ISOLATED_VIDEO_COLUMN, \"\")).strip() or path.stem\n",
    "            signer = str(row.get(ISOLATED_SIGNER_COLUMN, \"\")).strip() if ISOLATED_SIGNER_COLUMN else \"\"\n",
    "            records.append({\"features\": features, \"label\": label, \"video_id\": video, \"signer\": signer, \"path\": str(path)})\n",
    "        except Exception as exc:\n",
    "            errors.append(f\"row {index + 2} ({path}): {exc}\")\n",
    "    if errors:\n",
    "        print(f\"Invalid recognition samples: {len(errors)}\")\n",
    "        print(\"\\n\".join(errors[:20]))\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"Recognition data validation failed; no samples were silently discarded.\")\n",
    "    if len(records) < 3:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"Need at least three valid recognition samples, found {len(records)}\")\n",
    "    labels = sorted({row[\"label\"] for row in records})\n",
    "    if len(labels) < 2:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"Need at least two isolated-sign classes, found {labels}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"recognition rows={len(records)}; classes={len(labels)}; labels={labels}\")\n",
    "    return records\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def convert_isl_csltr_to_canonical_manifest(\n",
    "    video_dir, sentence_mapping_path, output_manifest_path,\n",
    "    signer_mapping=None\n",
    "):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Convert an attached ISL-CSLTR Mendeley dataset into the canonical translation manifest.\n",
    "\n",
    "    ISL-CSLTR (10.17632/kcmpdxky7p.1) contains 700 continuous sign videos across 7 signers\n",
    "    and 100 sentences. This function matches existing video files to sentence targets and\n",
    "    writes a canonical translation CSV:\n",
    "        pose_path,text,video_id,split,signer\n",
    "\n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        video_dir: Directory containing ISL-CSLTR video files or extracted landmarks.\n",
    "        sentence_mapping_path: CSV or text file mapping video/sentence identifiers to English sentences.\n",
    "        output_manifest_path: Destination path for the canonical CSV.\n",
    "        signer_mapping: Optional dict mapping video identifiers to signer IDs.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    video_dir = Path(video_dir)\n",
    "    sentence_mapping_path = Path(sentence_mapping_path)\n",
    "    output_manifest_path = Path(output_manifest_path)\n",
    "\n",
    "    if not video_dir.is_dir():\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"ISL-CSLTR video directory not found: {video_dir}\")\n",
    "    if not sentence_mapping_path.is_file():\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Sentence mapping file not found: {sentence_mapping_path}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Read sentences mapping\n",
    "    mapping = {}\n",
    "    with sentence_mapping_path.open(newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8-sig\") as stream:\n",
    "        sample_line = stream.readline()\n",
    "        stream.seek(0)\n",
    "        delimiter = \",\" if \",\" in sample_line else (\"\\t\" if \"\\t\" in sample_line else None)\n",
    "        reader = csv.reader(stream, delimiter=delimiter) if delimiter else csv.reader(stream)\n",
    "        for row in reader:\n",
    "            if len(row) >= 2:\n",
    "                key, text = row[0].strip(), row[1].strip()\n",
    "                if key and text:\n",
    "                    mapping[key] = text\n",
    "                    mapping[Path(key).stem] = text\n",
    "\n",
    "    if not mapping:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"No valid mappings found in {sentence_mapping_path}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Discover video / pose files\n",
    "    video_files = [p for p in video_dir.rglob(\"*\") if p.is_file() and p.suffix.lower() in (\".mp4\", \".mov\", \".pose\", \".npy\", \".npz\")]\n",
    "    if not video_files:\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"No video or pose files found in {video_dir}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    records = []\n",
    "    missing = []\n",
    "    for vpath in video_files:\n",
    "        stem = vpath.stem\n",
    "        text = mapping.get(stem) or mapping.get(vpath.name)\n",
    "        if text is None:\n",
    "            # Check if filename encodes sentence id, e.g. sentence_001\n",
    "            for k in mapping:\n",
    "                if k in stem:\n",
    "                    text = mapping[k]\n",
    "                    break\n",
    "        if text:\n",
    "            # Attempt to extract signer ID from filename or directory structure\n",
    "            signer = \"\"\n",
    "            if signer_mapping and stem in signer_mapping:\n",
    "                signer = signer_mapping[stem]\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                for part in stem.split(\"_\") + [p.name for p in vpath.parents]:\n",
    "                    if part.lower().startswith(\"signer\") or (part.lower().startswith(\"s\") and part[1:].isdigit()):\n",
    "                        signer = part\n",
    "                        break\n",
    "            video_id = stem\n",
    "            records.append({\n",
    "                \"pose_path\": str(vpath.resolve()),\n",
    "                \"text\": text,\n",
    "                \"video_id\": video_id,\n",
    "                \"split\": \"\",  # let assign_translation_splits handle split by signer/video\n",
    "                \"signer\": signer,\n",
    "            })\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            missing.append(str(vpath))\n",
    "\n",
    "    records.sort(key=lambda r: (r[\"signer\"], r[\"video_id\"]))\n",
    "    if not records:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"None of the {len(video_files)} video files could be matched to sentences in {sentence_mapping_path}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    output_manifest_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    with output_manifest_path.open(\"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as stream:\n",
    "        writer = csv.DictWriter(stream, fieldnames=[\"pose_path\", \"text\", \"video_id\", \"split\", \"signer\"])\n",
    "        writer.writeheader()\n",
    "        writer.writerows(records)\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f\"Generated ISL-CSLTR canonical manifest: {output_manifest_path}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Aligned samples: {len(records)}; unmatched files: {len(missing)}\")\n",
    "    return output_manifest_path\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "recognition",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Model A: isolated sign recognition\n",
    "\n",
    "This temporal Conv1d classifier mirrors the current backend's 64×225 feature contract and `IsolatedWordNet` checkpoint shape. Labels remain local to the selected dataset. Validation data selects the best checkpoint; test metrics are calculated only after model selection."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "recognition-model",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class IsolatedWordNet(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, class_count):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.layers = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Conv1d(225, 64, kernel_size=5, padding=2),\n",
    "            nn.GELU(),\n",
    "            nn.Conv1d(64, 96, kernel_size=3, padding=1),\n",
    "            nn.GELU(),\n",
    "            nn.AdaptiveAvgPool1d(1),\n",
    "            nn.Flatten(),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(96, class_count),\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, features):\n",
    "        return self.layers(features.transpose(1, 2))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def classification_metrics(y_true, y_pred, class_count, train_classes=None):\n",
    "    matrix = np.zeros((class_count, class_count), dtype=np.int64)\n",
    "    for truth, pred in zip(y_true, y_pred):\n",
    "        matrix[int(truth), int(pred)] += 1\n",
    "    precision, recall, f1 = [], [], []\n",
    "    for i in range(class_count):\n",
    "        tp = int(matrix[i, i])\n",
    "        pden, rden = int(matrix[:, i].sum()), int(matrix[i, :].sum())\n",
    "        p = tp / pden if pden else 0.0\n",
    "        r = tp / rden if rden else 0.0\n",
    "        precision.append(p)\n",
    "        recall.append(r)\n",
    "        f1.append(2 * p * r / (p + r) if p + r else 0.0)\n",
    "    accuracy = float(np.trace(matrix) / max(matrix.sum(), 1))\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Evaluate seen vs. unseen classes if training split classes were provided\n",
    "    unseen_in_train = []\n",
    "    seen_f1 = []\n",
    "    if train_classes is not None:\n",
    "        train_set = set(train_classes)\n",
    "        unseen_in_train = sorted(set(range(class_count)) - train_set)\n",
    "        seen_f1 = [f1[i] for i in train_set if i < class_count]\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"accuracy\": accuracy,\n",
    "        \"macro_precision\": float(np.mean(precision)),\n",
    "        \"macro_recall\": float(np.mean(recall)),\n",
    "        \"macro_f1\": float(np.mean(f1)),\n",
    "        \"seen_classes_macro_f1\": float(np.mean(seen_f1)) if seen_f1 else float(np.mean(f1)),\n",
    "        \"unseen_classes_in_training\": unseen_in_train,\n",
    "        \"per_class_recall\": {str(i): recall[i] for i in range(class_count)},\n",
    "        \"confusion_matrix\": matrix.tolist(),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def atomic_torch_save(payload, path):\n",
    "    path = Path(path)\n",
    "    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    temporary = path.with_name(path.name + \".tmp\")\n",
    "    torch.save(payload, temporary)\n",
    "    os.replace(temporary, path)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def atomic_json_save(payload, path):\n",
    "    path = Path(path)\n",
    "    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    temporary = path.with_name(path.name + \".tmp\")\n",
    "    temporary.write_text(json.dumps(payload, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
    "    os.replace(temporary, path)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _tuple_tree(value):\n",
    "    return tuple(_tuple_tree(item) for item in value) if isinstance(value, list) else value\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def capture_rng_state():\n",
    "    name, keys, position, has_gauss, cached = np.random.get_state()\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"python_rng_json\": json.dumps(random.getstate()),\n",
    "        \"numpy_rng\": {\"name\": name, \"keys\": keys.tolist(), \"position\": position,\n",
    "                      \"has_gauss\": has_gauss, \"cached_gaussian\": cached},\n",
    "        \"torch_rng\": torch.get_rng_state(),\n",
    "        \"cuda_rng\": torch.cuda.get_rng_state_all() if torch.cuda.is_available() else None,\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def restore_rng_state(state):\n",
    "    random.setstate(_tuple_tree(json.loads(state[\"python_rng_json\"])))\n",
    "    numpy_rng = state[\"numpy_rng\"]\n",
    "    np.random.set_state((numpy_rng[\"name\"], np.asarray(numpy_rng[\"keys\"], dtype=np.uint32),\n",
    "                         numpy_rng[\"position\"], numpy_rng[\"has_gauss\"], numpy_rng[\"cached_gaussian\"]))\n",
    "    torch.set_rng_state(state[\"torch_rng\"])\n",
    "    if torch.cuda.is_available() and state.get(\"cuda_rng\") is not None:\n",
    "        torch.cuda.set_rng_state_all(state[\"cuda_rng\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _classification_eval(model, loader, class_count, train_classes=None):\n",
    "    model.eval()\n",
    "    truths, predictions, total_loss, total = [], [], 0.0, 0\n",
    "    with torch.inference_mode():\n",
    "        for features, labels in loader:\n",
    "            logits = model(features.to(DEVICE))\n",
    "            total_loss += float(nn.functional.cross_entropy(logits, labels.to(DEVICE), reduction=\"sum\").item())\n",
    "            total += len(labels)\n",
    "            truths.extend(labels.tolist())\n",
    "            predictions.extend(logits.argmax(dim=1).cpu().tolist())\n",
    "    metrics = classification_metrics(truths, predictions, class_count, train_classes)\n",
    "    metrics[\"loss\"] = total_loss / max(total, 1)\n",
    "    return metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _classification_examples(model, rows, labels, limit=8):\n",
    "    examples = []\n",
    "    model.eval()\n",
    "    with torch.inference_mode():\n",
    "        for row in rows[:limit]:\n",
    "            logits = model(torch.from_numpy(row[\"features\"][None]).to(DEVICE))[0]\n",
    "            probabilities = torch.softmax(logits, dim=-1)\n",
    "            confidence, index = probabilities.max(dim=0)\n",
    "            examples.append({\n",
    "                \"path\": row[\"path\"], \"ground_truth\": row[\"label\"],\n",
    "                \"prediction\": labels[int(index)], \"confidence\": float(confidence),\n",
    "                \"accepted_at_backend_threshold\": float(confidence) >= 0.5,\n",
    "            })\n",
    "    return examples\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def train_recognition():\n",
    "    if not CONFIRM_DATASET_RIGHTS:\n",
    "        raise PermissionError(\"Confirm attached dataset rights in configuration before training.\")\n",
    "    if ISOLATED_LICENSE.strip().lower() in (\"\", \"unverified\", \"unknown\", \"none\"):\n",
    "        raise PermissionError(\"Set ISOLATED_LICENSE after verifying source terms; unresolved-license data is disabled.\")\n",
    "    records = load_isolated_records()\n",
    "    signer_complete = bool(ISOLATED_SIGNER_COLUMN) and all(r[\"signer\"] for r in records)\n",
    "    group_key = \"signer\" if signer_complete else \"video_id\"\n",
    "    if not signer_complete:\n",
    "        print(\"Signer metadata absent/incomplete: split is video-independent only; signer generalization is unverified.\")\n",
    "    split = split_grouped(records, group_key)\n",
    "    video_sets = {name: {r[\"video_id\"] for r in rows} for name, rows in split.items()}\n",
    "    if (video_sets[\"train\"] & video_sets[\"validation\"] or\n",
    "        video_sets[\"train\"] & video_sets[\"test\"] or\n",
    "        video_sets[\"validation\"] & video_sets[\"test\"]):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"Video leakage detected in recognition split.\")\n",
    "    split = {name: limit_split(rows, MAX_SAMPLES_PER_SPLIT, SEED + i) for i, (name, rows) in enumerate(split.items())}\n",
    "    labels = sorted({r[\"label\"] for r in records})\n",
    "    label_to_id = {label: i for i, label in enumerate(labels)}\n",
    "\n",
    "    train_class_indices = {label_to_id[r[\"label\"]] for r in split[\"train\"]}\n",
    "    absent_from_train = sorted(set(range(len(labels))) - train_class_indices)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Preflight Summary\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
    "    print(\"MODEL A: ISOLATED SIGN RECOGNITION PREFLIGHT SUMMARY\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
    "    print(f\"Total valid samples: {len(records):,}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Total vocabulary classes: {len(labels)}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Samples per split: {', '.join(f'{k}={len(v)}' for k, v in split.items())}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Class coverage by split:\")\n",
    "    for name, rows in split.items():\n",
    "        present = Counter(r['label'] for r in rows)\n",
    "        absent = sorted(set(labels) - set(present))\n",
    "        print(f\"  {name}: {len(present)}/{len(labels)} classes present ({len(rows)} samples)\")\n",
    "        if absent:\n",
    "            print(f\"    WARNING: {len(absent)} classes absent from {name} split: {absent[:6]}{'...' if len(absent) > 6 else ''}\")\n",
    "    if absent_from_train:\n",
    "        print(f\"CRITICAL: {len(absent_from_train)} classes are absent from the training split. Evaluation will track seen vs. unseen classes.\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Signer/video overlap:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  train & validation = {len(video_sets['train'] & video_sets['validation'])}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  train & test = {len(video_sets['train'] & video_sets['test'])}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  validation & test = {len(video_sets['validation'] & video_sets['test'])}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Feature dimensions: {records[0]['features'].shape} (64 frames x 225 coordinates)\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Dataset name: {ISOLATED_DATASET_NAME}; License: {ISOLATED_LICENSE}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Training mode: {TRAINING_MODE}; Scope: {TRAINING_SCOPE}\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def loader(rows, shuffle):\n",
    "        x = torch.from_numpy(np.stack([r[\"features\"] for r in rows]))\n",
    "        y = torch.tensor([label_to_id[r[\"label\"]] for r in rows], dtype=torch.long)\n",
    "        return DataLoader(TensorDataset(x, y), batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=shuffle)\n",
    "    train_loader = loader(split[\"train\"], True)\n",
    "    val_loader = loader(split[\"validation\"], False)\n",
    "    train_eval_loader = loader(split[\"train\"], False)\n",
    "    output = OUTPUT_ROOT / \"recognition\"\n",
    "    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    state_path = output / \"training_state.pt\"\n",
    "    model_path = output / \"model.pt\"\n",
    "    if RESUME_RECOGNITION:\n",
    "        if not state_path.is_file():\n",
    "            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Resume requested but no recovery checkpoint exists: {state_path}\")\n",
    "    elif state_path.exists() or model_path.exists():\n",
    "        raise FileExistsError(f\"Output exists at {output}; set RESUME_RECOGNITION=True to resume, or choose another output.\")\n",
    "    model = IsolatedWordNet(len(labels)).to(DEVICE)\n",
    "    optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=LEARNING_RATE)\n",
    "    history, best_f1, start_epoch = [], -1.0, 0\n",
    "    data_fingerprint = fingerprint_rows(records, (\"path\", \"label\", \"video_id\", \"signer\"))\n",
    "    training_config = {\"batch_size\": BATCH_SIZE, \"learning_rate\": LEARNING_RATE,\n",
    "                       \"seed\": SEED, \"max_samples_per_split\": MAX_SAMPLES_PER_SPLIT,\n",
    "                       \"training_mode\": TRAINING_MODE, \"training_scope\": TRAINING_SCOPE}\n",
    "    if RESUME_RECOGNITION:\n",
    "        state = torch.load(state_path, map_location=DEVICE, weights_only=True)\n",
    "        if (state[\"labels\"] != labels or state[\"group_key\"] != group_key\n",
    "                or state[\"data_fingerprint\"] != data_fingerprint\n",
    "                or state[\"training_config\"] != training_config):\n",
    "            raise ValueError(\"Recognition checkpoint data contract differs from current manifest.\")\n",
    "        model.load_state_dict(state[\"state_dict\"])\n",
    "        optimizer.load_state_dict(state[\"optimizer\"])\n",
    "        history, best_f1, start_epoch = state[\"history\"], state[\"best_f1\"], state[\"epoch\"] + 1\n",
    "        restore_rng_state(state)\n",
    "    if EPOCHS <= 0:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"EPOCHS must be positive.\")\n",
    "    for epoch in range(start_epoch, EPOCHS):\n",
    "        model.train()\n",
    "        total_loss, total, correct = 0.0, 0, 0\n",
    "        for features, targets in train_loader:\n",
    "            features, targets = features.to(DEVICE), targets.to(DEVICE)\n",
    "            optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n",
    "            logits = model(features)\n",
    "            loss = nn.functional.cross_entropy(logits, targets)\n",
    "            loss.backward()\n",
    "            optimizer.step()\n",
    "            total_loss += float(loss.item()) * len(targets)\n",
    "            total += len(targets)\n",
    "            correct += int((logits.argmax(1) == targets).sum())\n",
    "        val = _classification_eval(model, val_loader, len(labels), train_class_indices)\n",
    "        row = {\"epoch\": epoch + 1, \"train_loss\": total_loss / max(total, 1),\n",
    "               \"train_accuracy\": correct / max(total, 1), \"validation_accuracy\": val[\"accuracy\"],\n",
    "               \"validation_loss\": val[\"loss\"], \"validation_macro_f1\": val[\"macro_f1\"],\n",
    "               \"validation_seen_classes_macro_f1\": val[\"seen_classes_macro_f1\"]}\n",
    "        history.append(row)\n",
    "        if val[\"macro_f1\"] > best_f1:\n",
    "            best_f1 = val[\"macro_f1\"]\n",
    "            atomic_torch_save({\"state_dict\": model.state_dict()}, model_path)\n",
    "        atomic_torch_save({\n",
    "            \"state_dict\": model.state_dict(), \"optimizer\": optimizer.state_dict(),\n",
    "            \"epoch\": epoch, \"best_f1\": best_f1, \"history\": history, \"labels\": labels,\n",
    "            \"group_key\": group_key, \"data_fingerprint\": data_fingerprint,\n",
    "            \"training_config\": training_config, **capture_rng_state(),\n",
    "        }, state_path)\n",
    "        print(row)\n",
    "    model.load_state_dict(torch.load(model_path, map_location=DEVICE, weights_only=True)[\"state_dict\"])\n",
    "    test_loader = loader(split[\"test\"], False)\n",
    "    test_metrics = _classification_eval(model, test_loader, len(labels), train_class_indices)\n",
    "    report = {\n",
    "        \"status\": \"EXPERIMENTAL_NOT_PROMOTED\",\n",
    "        \"scope\": TRAINING_SCOPE,\n",
    "        \"training_mode\": TRAINING_MODE,\n",
    "        \"dataset\": ISOLATED_DATASET_NAME, \"license\": ISOLATED_LICENSE,\n",
    "        \"signer_independent\": signer_complete, \"split_group\": group_key,\n",
    "        \"rows\": {name: len(rows) for name, rows in split.items()},\n",
    "        \"training\": _classification_eval(model, train_eval_loader, len(labels), train_class_indices),\n",
    "        \"validation\": _classification_eval(model, val_loader, len(labels), train_class_indices),\n",
    "        \"test\": test_metrics,\n",
    "        \"representative_predictions\": _classification_examples(\n",
    "            model, split[\"test\"], labels\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        \"history\": history,\n",
    "        \"classes_absent_from_training\": [labels[i] for i in absent_from_train],\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    atomic_json_save(report, output / \"evaluation_results.json\")\n",
    "    atomic_json_save(labels, output / \"labels.json\")\n",
    "    model_config = {\"architecture\": \"IsolatedWordNet\", \"class_count\": len(labels),\n",
    "                    \"input_shape\": [64, 225], \"feature_version\": \"pose_hands_root_scale_v1\",\n",
    "                    \"training_scope\": TRAINING_SCOPE, \"seed\": SEED}\n",
    "    preprocess = {\"source_shape\": [None, 543, 3], \"selected_landmarks\": \"pose 0:33 + hands 501:543\",\n",
    "                  \"frames\": 64, \"features_per_frame\": 225, \"normalization\": \"hip-center / median shoulder width\"}\n",
    "    digest = hashlib.sha256(model_path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n",
    "    metadata = {\n",
    "        \"format\": \"signsage_isolated_words_v1\", \"labels\": labels,\n",
    "        \"feature_version\": \"pose_hands_root_scale_v1\", \"feature_dim\": 225,\n",
    "        \"confidence_threshold\": 0.5, \"checkpoint_sha256\": digest,\n",
    "        \"evaluation\": report, \"promotion_eligible\": False,\n",
    "        \"dataset\": ISOLATED_DATASET_NAME, \"license\": ISOLATED_LICENSE,\n",
    "        \"raw_videos_included\": False,\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    atomic_json_save(model_config, output / \"model_config.json\")\n",
    "    atomic_json_save(preprocess, output / \"preprocessing_config.json\")\n",
    "    atomic_json_save(metadata, output / \"metadata.json\")\n",
    "    atomic_json_save(history, output / \"training_history.json\")\n",
    "    print(\"Recognition held-out test:\", report[\"test\"])\n",
    "    if absent_from_train:\n",
    "        print(f\"Note: test macro_f1 includes {len(absent_from_train)} unseen classes. Seen-classes macro F1: {test_metrics['seen_classes_macro_f1']:.4f}\")\n",
    "    print(\"Recognition uncertainty: backend returns accepted=false below confidence threshold.\")\n",
    "    return report\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "if TRAIN_RECOGNITION:\n",
    "    RECOGNITION_REPORT = train_recognition()\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Model A training disabled. Attach a validated manifest and explicitly enable TRAIN_RECOGNITION.\")\n"
   ]
  },
